In React with React Router: use a `<Helmet>` (react‑helmet) or the `useDocumentTitle` hook.
In Vue with Vue Router: use `afterEach` to set `document.title`.
In Angular: set `title` property in route data and use a service.

```javascript
// Vue Router example
router.afterEach((to) => {
  document.title = to.meta.title || 'Default Title';
});
```

Always include the unique page title; screen readers announce it on focus.

